Z||000016||brianp1fiero||07-31-2000||10:15 PM||||I know this is like beating a dead horse, but I have, and installed a kit made by Gary Zumalt.  I bought it from him in 1994 to fit my GM ZZ3 crate engine.  There were no cuts made to any part of my frame to install his kit.  It also came with heavier drive axles for my A/T that were the proper length.  I have a "shorty" style water pump that resides inside the frame rail.  <p>[This message has been edited by brianp1fiero (edited 07-31-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000017||squid||08-01-2000||01:34 PM||||There are pluses and minuses to every kit. Two minuses to Zumalts kit are increased torque steer(from an even shorter left axle) and increased cost. The main reason I dont want the pulley in the wheel well is the additional cost of the drive system. I'm building this on a "shoe string". $610 for Archies partial v8 kit , $75 for a 4.3 junkyard engine, $150 for 4.10 4 spd, etc. I cant justify spending more than the cost of a mid 80's vette(@$5000 here)even if it is faster. To each his own. Its all good.||||reg||1
